   "description_book": "The Da Vinci Code is a 2003 mystery thriller novel by Dan Brown, featuring symbologist Robert Langdon and cryptologist Sophie Neveu. The story begins with a murder in the Louvre Museum in Paris, leading them into a conflict between the Priory of Sion and Opus Dei regarding the controversial idea that Jesus Christ and Mary Magdalene had a child together. The novel explores alternative religious history and has sparked significant debate and interest in the Holy Grail legend.",
