   "description_book": "Gaibéus is the debut novel of Alves Redol, published in 1939, marking the beginning of neo-realism in Portugal. The story focuses on the lives of peasants from the northern provinces of Ribatejo and Beira Baixa, who work in harsh conditions during the rice harvest, highlighting their struggles with poverty, disease, and exploitation, as well as their fleeting moments of joy and dreams for a better life. Redol's work aims to expose social inequalities and the exploitation of man by man.",
   "description_ban": "Banned in Portugal under Estado Novo because of its socialist themes and critique of rural exploitation.",
